   This is the version 3.00 of gnuchess for OSK. To use it, move the archiveto directory /h0/usr/src/chess and unpack it. Change the attributes of gnu-chess, gnuchessn and gnuchessr to -pe -pr -e.   Should the memory become insufficient, change the size of "ttblsz" infile gnuchess.h to a smaller power of 2 (like 4096) and remake the programs.   The programs have been compiled with the standard Microware C compilerand made with Microware's make. There exists a newer version (3.1) whichneeds the GNU C compiler.   If you want to have the programs in a directory different from/h0/usr/src/chess, change this pathname in the Makefile and in files *dsp.cand remake the program.   This program uses the libraries os9lib.l and ncurses.l, and also some headerfiles (ncurses.h, signal.h) from the TOP group, available on hermit.cs.wisc.edu.Makefile assumes that the libraries are in /dd/lib.   The X-windows graphics interface XCHESS sources are included (untouched).The challenge is to convert them into a graphics/mouse interface for MM/1.   Andrzej Kotanski(kotanski@zeus02.desy.de)Cracow, May 2, 1992.